# The C gate's analysis, run by the build on every target of the project (cmake/lint-gate.cmake):
# a finding is an error. The checks that find a defect are on, and only them: the static analyzer, the
# bugprone and cert families, and the checks listed one by one from the other families. The checks of
# style, of naming and of micro-optimization are not here: they find no defect, and on code that exists
# they only make it be rewritten. Off in the analyzer: the demand for the bounds-checked functions of
# C11's Annex K (snprintf_s) — glibc and musl do not provide them, so every snprintf would fail with no
# replacement to write. A check joins or leaves the list by the project owner's decision, with its reason.
Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,-bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  cert-*,
  misc-redundant-expression,misc-misplaced-const,misc-definitions-in-headers,misc-non-copyable-objects,
  misc-misleading-bidirectional,misc-misleading-identifier,
  readability-misleading-indentation
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*'
